# TargetCore exported surface -- the flat C ABI. THE COVERED SURFACE.
#
# Generated from TargetCore_c.h (every declaration marked P2PC_API), names only,
# sorted. Regenerate with:
#     python .github/ci/check_repo_invariants.py --regenerate-abi
#
# This file IS the promise. The versioning policy is written in terms
# of it: a name here is covered, a name absent from it is not, and a removal is
# a MAJOR bump once the project is 1.0. Editing it is the moment to decide
# whether a new entry point is a promise worth making -- which is why the check
# fails on an undeclared addition rather than absorbing it.
#
# Checked twice, and it needs both. check_repo_invariants.py compares this list
# against the header with no compiler involved; ctest -R p2p_abisurface compares
# it against the symbols the BUILT library actually exports, on both platforms.
# The header can promise a symbol the library does not export -- that is a link
# error for a consumer and nothing here would otherwise see it.

